__newline_3     Three Categorial Symmetry Principles for Robust AGI Motivation_newline_To explicate the structure and meaning of the category-theoretic setup at the heart of MetaMo, we_newline_articulate three _quote_meta-motivational_quote_ symmetry principles trivially derived therefrom._newline__newline_3.1   First Principle: Modular Appraisal-Decision Interface_newline_                                         λX          _newline_                               Ψ D(X)          D Ψ (X)_newline__newline_                                      Ψ (µX )                      µΨ (X)_newline__newline__newline_                                          Ψ (X)       λX_newline_                                                               D(X)_newline_4       Ruiting Lian and Ben Goertzel_newline__newline_   Basic concept: You can swap updating ”how you feel” and choosing ”what to do” in_newline_either order and still end up in essentially the same state._newline__newline__newline_Technical Explanation Appraisal (Ψ ) and decision (D) each carry side-effects on disjoint state_newline_channels (feelings vs. goal intensities). The law λ asserts that running appraisal then decision_newline_differs only by a controlled distortion from running decision then appraisal. Because these distortions_newline_compose in the quantale (Q, ⊗), one can nest and interleave any number of appraisal/decision cycles_newline_while still preserving overall coherence: you can fold multiple ”feel-then-choose” or ”choose-then-feel”_newline_steps into a single update without contradiction._newline__newline__newline_ Technical Explanation For those interested in the categorial infrastructure, a few more details_newline_follow. If we let (Q, ≤, ⊗, e) be a commutative quantale and C a Q-enriched symmetric monoidal_newline_bicategory, then a lax comonad Ψ and a lax monad D on C are each equipped with unit and tensor_newline_2-cells ψX,Y : Ψ (X) ⊗ Ψ (Y ) → Ψ (X ⊗ Y ), dX,Y : D(X) ⊗ D(Y ) → D(X ⊗ Y ), satisf