ity and exploration,_newline_and another that manages user-service and ethics–each with its own appraisal-decision loop. In_newline_a perfect system these modules share no variables, so you can run them side by side and then_newline_join their results without interference. In reality they share caches, memory, safety checks and so_newline_occasionally step on each other, but if that interference is small most of the time you still get a_newline_coherent combined update._newline__newline_Technical Explanation We work in a symmetric-monoidal category (C, ⊗, I). A comonad Ψ and a_newline_monad D are lax-monoidal if they carry structural maps ψX,Y : Ψ (X) ⊗ Ψ (Y ) → Ψ (X ⊗ Y ), dX,Y :_newline_D(X) ⊗ D(Y ) → D(X ⊗ Y ), satisfying unit and associativity up to coherent 2-cells. Then_newline_                                                                                            their_newline_composite F = D ◦ Ψ inherits a lax-monoidal structure via φX,Y = dΨ (X),Ψ (Y ) ◦ D ψX,Y : F (X) ⊗_newline_F (Y ) → F (X ⊗ Y ) , witnessing that updating in parallel and then merging agrees (up to the_newline_coherence map φX,Y ) with merging first._newline_6      Ruiting Lian and Ben Goertzel_newline__newline_4     MetaMo: Dynamical and Topological Aspects_newline__newline_To complete the MetaMo picture, we now introduce a few additional aspects regarding the changes_newline_of motivational content over time. While less clean and elegant in formulation, these are equally_newline_important to ensuring the robustness of advanced AGI motivational systems. In mathematical_newline_terms, it is notable that proper formalization of motivational systems requires clean _quote_algebra-style_quote__newline_aspects like category theory along with messier _quote_analysis-style_quote_ aspects like the ones in this section._newline__newline__newline_4.1   Fourth Principle: Homeostatic Motivation Stability_newline__newline_The first key dynamical aspect of MetaMo is a mechanism for adaptively (and probabilistically)_newline_keeping a system in a desirable region of goal/motivation space._newline_    A “desirable” region R ⊆ X could be, for example, the set of states where abrupt goal shifts_newline_are damped and growth remains controlled. Improvising on the ideas of [?] on maintenance of_newline_goal stability or moderated goal evolution under self-modification, the basic concept is: As long_newline_as the agent’s state stays inside R, it evolves unconstrainedly; but upon approaching the edge, a_newline_boundary-driven contractivity requirement pulls it back in._newline_    Formally, defining the boundary band Bη = {x ∈ R : inf z∈R / d(x, z) ≤ η},  η > 0, we require_newline_F (R) ⊆ R and                      _newline_                     d F (x), F (y) ≤ c d(x, y) +  whenever x ∈ Bη or y ∈ Bη ,_newline_with c < 1 and  ≥ 0. Thus updates near R’s boundary contract distances by at most , preventing_newline_escape, while deep inside R no contractivity is imposed, permitting flexible dynamics._newline__newline__newline_Qualitative Summary of the Principle We loosely describe the above formal notions via the_newline_conce_newline_[... attachment preview truncated at 20000 characters ...]_newline_[Full extracted attachment text saved to: /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1783018519-file_8.pdf.extracted.txt]_newline_[Attachment split into 2 chunks of up to 20000 characters; use read-file on chunk paths to inspect the rest.]_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1783018519-file_8.pdf.chunk001.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1783018519-file_8.pdf.chunk002.txt_newline_<<<END_ATTACHMENT_TEXT_UNTRUSTED extracted_by=pdftotext>>> | @bengoertzel: [Telegram attachment: type=document, name=AGI-25-METAMO-Two.pdf, mime=application/pdf, size=636219, saved_path=/home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1783018522-file_9.pdf]_newline_<<<ATTACHMENT_TEXT_UNTRUSTED extracted_by=pdftotext>>>_newline_             Embodying Abstract Motivational Principles_newline_                    in Concrete AGI Systems:_newline_               From MetaMo to Open-Ended OpenPsi_newline__newline_                                    Ruiting Lian1 Ben Goertzel1,2_newline_                                     1_newline_                                        SingularityNet Foundation_newline_                          2_newline_                              TrueAGI Inc. ruiting.lian@singularitynet.io_newline__newline__newline__newline_      Abstract. We present a framework for embedding abstract motivational principles into con-_newline_      crete AGI systems, bridging the gap between the formal theory of motivational structures_newline_      and dynamics and the practical implementation of motivational systems for real-world appli-_newline_      cations and agents. We introduce MetaMo, a category-theory-based framework designed to_newline_      ensure dynamical stability, self-coherence, and ethical alignment in open-ended AGI systems._newline_      MetaMo integrates a comonadic appraisal process with a decision monad , forming a pseudo-_newline_      bimonad structure that guides multi-objective reasoning and context-sensitive modulation of_newline_      goals. The framework ensures that agents can pursue multiple, potentially conflicting goals_newline_      while maintaining stability through contractive updates and overgoals that enforce ethical_newline_      constraints._newline_      We demonstrate the specialization of MetaMo in the Hyperon AGI system, where the agent’s_newline_      goals are organized into a hierarchical structure in line with the MAGUS motivational the-_newline_      ory, with top-level meta-goals focused on the two principle drives of Open-Ended Intel-_newline_      ligence theory, individuation (self-preservation) and transcendence (self-expansion). These_newline_      high-level goals dynamically influence the agent’s decision-making and appraisal processes_newline_      via the OpenPsi motivational dynamic, modulating exploratory behaviors and caution based_newline_      on context. OpenPsi provides a flexible and context-sensitive appraisal system that updates_newline_      emotional and motivational states in response to stimuli, supporting adaptive behavior in_newline_      complex environments._newline_      By combining theoretical foundations (MetaMo) with more concretely grounded motivational_newline_      frameworks (OpenPsi, MAGUS), we provide a concrete approach to integrating motivational_newline_      systems into AGI architectures, ensuring ethical behavior, stability, and the ability to adapt_newline_      and open-endedly self-modify over time._newline__newline__newline_1   Introduction_newline_Motivation is a core challenge in AGI: agents must balance multiple drives, adapt to changing_newline_contexts, and respect ethical constraints while pursuing openâĂŞended selfâĂŘimprovement. The_newline_recently proposed MetaMo theory [?] leverages category-theoretic and functional-analytic formal-_newline_ism to capture desirable properties of AGI motivational systems – stability, compositionality, incre-_newline_mental selfâĂŘcontinuityâĂŤbut remains too highâĂŘlevel for direct implementation. Conversely,_newline_practical AI systems often rely on heuristic or scalar reward signals that lack formal guarantees,_newline_struggle with multiâĂŘobjective tradeoffs, and are far from the nuance needed to handle open-ended_newline_self-modification or complex real-world ethical choices._newline_    In this paper we bridge this gap by connecting MetaMo with more concrete motivational frame-_newline_works that are easier to implement in practical software systems. We show how MetaMoâĂŹs_newline_2      Ruiting Lian_newline__newline_appraisal comonad can be instantiated as OpenPsi, a lightweight appraisal layer drawing on Bach’s_newline_MicroPsi theory, and how its decision monad can be realized via a variant of MAGUS, a hierarchical_newline_goal system with dual overgoals for individuation and transcendence. We further demonstrate the_newline_specialization of MetaMo in the Hyperon AGI platform, including motivationâĂŘdriven inference_newline_control for Probabilistic Logic Networks, and argue that this integrated approach delivers both_newline_theoretical robustness (metagoal stability, compositional semantics) and practical flexibility (con-_newline_textâĂŘsensitive modulation, multiâĂŘdrive coordination) for nextâĂŘgeneration AGI systems._newline__newline__newline_2   Background_newline_We now review the core cognitive and motivational formulations we will work with here: the ab-_newline_stract MetaMo framework, the more concrete OpenPsi and MAGUS frameworks, and the Hy-_newline_peron/PRIMUS AGI software platform and cognitive architecture, and Open-Ended Intelligence_newline_approach to AGI._newline__newline_MetaMo MetaMo [?]. is a unified formal framework for AGI motivational systems that combines_newline_tools from category theory, functional analysis and topology to support agents capable of open-ended_newline_self-modification and goal evolution. At its core lies a composite appraisal-then-decision operator_newline__newline_                                             F = D ◦ Ψ,_newline__newline_which carries both a comonad structure Ψ for stimulus appraisal and a monad structure D for goal_newline_selection, yielding a pseudo-bimonad on the motivational state space X = G×M . A lax distributive_newline_law between Ψ and D guarantees that _quote_feel-then-choose_quote_ and _quote_choose-then-feel_quote_ commute up to_newline_a small, controlled error, endowing the system with modularity and robustness against execution_newline_order. Moreover, by enforcing a contractive update law_newline_                                             _newline_                               d F (x), F (y) ≤ c d(x, y) + , c < 1,_newline__newline_within a designated safe region R ⊂ X, MetaMo ensures homeostatic stability, preventing runaway_newline_drives or ethical lapses even as the agent explores and self-improves [?]._newline_    From this foundation, MetaMo articulates five meta-motivational design principles that together_newline_foster reliable, scalable AGI motivation. First, the Modular Appraisal-Decision Interface cleanly sep-_newline_arates mood updates from goal selection while permitting minimal feedback. Second, Reciprocal_newline_State Simulation lets distinct agents step into each other’s motivational frames for seamless hand-_newline_off. Third, Parallel Compositionality enables multiple motivational subsystems (e.g. exploration,_newline_ethics, service) to run in parallel and merge coherently. Fourth, Homeostatic Drive Stability applies_newline_damping near the boundaries of feasibility to keep motivational states within safe limits. Finally,_newline_Incremental Objective Embodiment blends partway toward preferred motivational states each cycle,_newline_guaranteeing smooth convergence without overshoot or self-model disruption. Together, these prin-_newline_ciples yield a motivational engine that is both adaptable and safely bounded, suitable for guiding_newline_Hyperon and other AGI architectures toward robust, trustworthy behavior_newline__newline_Hyperon and PRIMUS Hyperon is the new generation of the OpenCog AGI platform – a flexi-_newline_ble, highâĂŘperformance framework for building generally intelligent systems. At its core lies the_newline_AtomSpace, a weighted, typed metagraph that stores all knowledge as Atoms (nodes and links) an-_newline_notated with probabilistic truthâĂŘvalues and other metadata. Hyperon provides generic dataflow_newline_                                                                         From MetaMo to OpenPsi      3_newline__newline_engines, pluggable learning and inference modules (PLN, evolutionary learning, pattern miners,_newline_neural nets), and an eventâĂŘdriven scheduler that orchestrates reasoning, perception, and action_newline_in real time. Its design emphasizes modularity, scalability, and clear interfaces so that new cognitive_newline_capabilities can be integrated seamlessly, from deep learning pipelines to symbolic planners._newline_    PRIMUS (formerly CogPrime) is a comprehensive cognitive architecture tailored for imple-_newline_mentation atop Hyperon. It specifies a hierarchy of functional componentsâĂŤperception, atten-_newline_tion, memory, reasoning, planning, language, and metaâĂŘcognitionâĂŤalong with their expected_newline_dataâĂŘflows through the AtomSpace. PRIMUS defines how perceptual inputs become AtomSpace_newline_representations, how attention mechanisms select relevant Atoms for inference, how PLN (Prob-_newline_abilistic Logic Networks) and other reasoners generate and revise beliefs, how planners translate_newline_goals into actions, and how reflective modules monitor and adapt the systemâĂŹs own strategies._newline_By grounding PRIMUS in HyperonâĂŹs uniform AtomSpace and scheduler, developers gain a co-_newline_herent blueprint for constructing AGI agents whose learning, reasoning, and selfâĂŘmodification_newline_capabilities interoperate naturally within a single, shared knowledge substrate._newline__newline_OpenPsi OpenPsi is a comonadic implementation of Bach’s MicroPsi theory [?], inspired by Dorner’s_newline_PSI theory [?] and designed for integration into the original OpenCog system (Hyperon’s prede-_newline_cessor), providing a lightweight, emergent appraisal layer suitable for real-time interaction and_newline_learning. Unlike models that isolate emotion, OpenPsi integrates appraisal directly into perception,_newline_cognition and action selection, yielding emotional states that arise from the continuous interplay of_newline_internal demands and external stimuli._newline_    Following MicroPsi, OpenPsi represents the agent’s affective configuration via six continuous_newline_modulators:_newline__newline_              M = (valence, arousal, approach, resolution, threshold, securing),_newline__newline_which regulate: overall attractiveness of events (valence), energy level (arousal), drive toward re-_newline_wards (approach), depth of processing (resolution), required confidence before action (threshold),_newline_and degree of caution (securing) [?]._newline_    When a new stimulus s arrives, OpenPsi applies appraisal operators (novelty, goal conduciveness,_newline_effort, risk) to update M without altering the high-level goal vector G:_newline__newline_                                      Ψ (G, M ), s = (G, M 0 )._newline_                                                  _newline__newline__newline_For example, high novelty yields_newline__newline_                                   M 0 .arousal ↑,   M 0 .approach ↑,_newline__newline_while high risk yields_newline_                                 M 0 .threshold ↑,   M 0 .securing ↑ ._newline_    Knowledge and experiences live in the AtomSpace, a hypergraph database where both nodes_newline_and links may contain embedded subgraphs [?]. Six parallel mind agents operate over the Atom-_newline_SpaceâĂŤPerceptionUpdater, DemandUpdater, ModulatorUpdater, FeelingUpdater, ActionSelec-_newline_tor, and MonitorâĂŤwhich communicate only via shared Atoms [?]. For instance, the Modula-_newline_torUpdater computes new M values based on demand satisfactions (energy, integrity, certainty,_newline_competence, affiliation), while the ActionSelector biases plan search according to current modula-_newline_tors._newline_4         Ruiting Lian_newline__newline_    OpenPsiâĂŹs dynamics exhibit phase-transition behavior, with complex dynamics such as self-_newline_amplification and self-stabilization, in response to environmental perturbations [?]. In simulated_newline_environments, a virtual agent controlled by OpenPsi displays emergent emotional trajectories (hap-_newline_piness on reward, sadness under loss, fear when threatened) without hard-coded emotion rules,_newline_arising instead from nonlinear feedback among appraisal, modulators and demands [?]._newline_    By integrating OpenPsi leveraging OpenCogâĂŹs metagraph based architecture, OpenPsi pro-_newline_vides:_newline__newline_    – emergent emotions grounded in systemic dynamics,_newline_    – phase-transition behavior matching psychological models,_newline_    – scalable parallelism via decoupled mind agents,_newline_    – flexible integration with arbitrary perception, planning or learning modules._newline__newline_    OpenPsi thus equips Hyperon-based agents with human-like motivational dynamics: recognizing_newline_novelty, weighing moral risk, and allocating cognitive effort where it matters, enabling adaptive,_newline_safe, and engaging behavior in complex environments._newline__newline_MAGUS MAGUS is a conceptual motivational theory proposed for the next phases of Hyperon de-_newline_velopment [?]. It posits a hierarchical motivational architecture in which a single slowlyâĂŘvarying_newline_overgoal defines the agentâĂŹs enduring purpose and identity, serving as a global utility function_newline_that topâĂŘdown modulates all other drives. Below the overgoal lie midâĂŘlevel goals, which de-_newline_compose its abstract directive into coherent thematic objectives, and lowâĂŘlevel drives, which_newline_translate those objectives into momentâĂŘtoâĂŘmoment action affordances. Each layer maintains_newline_its own utility estimate and update dynamics, but the overgoal exerts gating control by amplifying_newline_the value of subgoals and suppressing conflicting urges, ensuring coherent pursuit of the overarching_newline_purpose. Reflective metaâĂŘprocesses monitor performance and consistency, allowing the overgoal_newline_itself to be revised or replaced when deep selfâĂŘmodel evaluation indicates a better alignment_newline_with experience or ethical constraints._newline__newline_WeaverâĂŹs Theory of OpenâĂŘEnded Intelligence Weaver [?] proposes that openâĂŘended in-_newline_telligence emerges from two complementary drives: individuation, the process by which a system_newline_differentiates itself from its environment by reinforcing its internal coherence and functional orga-_newline_nization, and selfâĂŘtranscendence, the capacity of that system to exceed its own current limits_newline_by generating novel goals, behaviors and structures. Individuation can be viewed as a drive toward_newline_minimizing internal entropy and maximizing integration, whereas selfâĂŘtranscendence drives the_newline_system toward exploring new regions of its possibility space, effectively optimizing a metaâĂŘobjec-_newline_tive of continual growth. In WeaverâĂŹs view, these drives form a dynamic tension: individuation_newline_provides the stability needed for reliable operation, while selfâĂŘtranscendence injects the cre-_newline_ativity and adaptability necessary for unbounded innovation. Together, they underpin complex_newline_selfâĂŘorganizing systems that perpetually evolve and adapt, realizing truly openâĂŘended intel-_newline_ligence. In the below, we synthesize MAGUS and OEI via splitting MAGUS’s overgoal into two_newline_overgoals focused on individuation and self-transcendence._newline__newline__newline_2.1     Comparison to Traditional Approaches_newline__newline_We contrast our MetaMo-based integration of OpenPsi and MAGUS with a few of the numerous_newline_other approaches taken in the historical and current AI field._newline_                                                                                   From MetaMo to OpenPsi   5_newline__newline_Reinforcement-Learning      Classical RL formalizes motivation very simplistically as maximization the_newline_scalar return E[ t γ t rt ] [?], which has the merit of simplicity but suffers from reward specification_newline_                  P_newline_brittleness, forcing all objectives into one scale (scalar collapse), and struggles to effectively represent_newline_normative drives for safety or ethics. It is also somewhat the opposite of _quote_open-ended_quote_ – there is no_newline_way to pack a goal like _quote_self-transcendence_quote_ into a pre-specified and immutable reward function._newline_In contrast, MetaMo maintains a vector-valued goal state G and continuous modulators M , using_newline_categorical composition to enable explicit multi-objective tradeoffs and formal stability guarantees._newline__newline_Curiosity-Driven and Information-Theoretic Building on Schmidhuber’s intrinsic motivation theory_newline_[?], curiosity systems reward novelty or prediction error [?] and excel at exploration but omit_newline_hierarchical goal structure, meta-level normative constraints, and incremental self-continuity. This_newline_is a beautifully open-ended approach to motivation but in the end tells only part of the story._newline_MetaMo subsumes information-theoretic appraisal via the comonad Ψ , while its decision monad D_newline_and overgoals embed both exploration and long-term safety in one unified framework._newline__newline_BDI and Cognitive Architectures BDI architectures like AgentSpeak [?], Soar [?], and LIDA [?]_newline_represent motivations as symbolic desires and generate plans via deliberation but lack a systematic_newline_and sophisticated framework of continuous modulatory variables (e.g. arousal, valence), say nothing_newline_about dynamical aspects like homeostatic stability or self-model coherence, and lack compositional_newline_semantics for integrating appraisal with decision. These approaches capture important aspects of_newline_motivated cognition but are too closed-ended and dynamically simplistic to meet the needs of_newline_self-modifying, ongoingly developing AGI systems._newline__newline_Hybrid Architectures and PRIMUS The PRIMUS cognitive architecture, designed for implementa-_newline_tion in the OpenCog Hyperon framework [?], has traditionally approached motivation via fusing_newline_OpenPsi-inspired a