g n + Op (log log n),_newline__newline_with posterior concentration approximated by a log-sum-exp dominance over neighborhoods. This_newline_is the first pillar: LLC as degeneracy / complexity penalty in learning dynamics._newline__newline_The conceptual gap. LLC is usually computed as a geometric invariant of a singular statistical_newline_model. Weakness, in contrast, is often introduced as an Occam-like preference for “indistinct”_newline_hypotheses, sometimes formalized using quantales with soft inf-convolution. The gap in many_newline_discussions is that weakness and LLC look related but live in different languages._newline__newline_The main move. We define weakness to be exactly (local) evidence, i.e. the same integral_newline_appearing in SLT. Then LLC is not approximated by weakness: it is the asymptotic log-volume_newline_exponent of weakness. To study composition and control, we place this evidence object in a_newline_thermodynamic quantale whose tropical (zero-temperature) limit becomes the min-plus semiring._newline_In that semiring, MAP over a refinement DAG of candidate factorizations is shortest-path dynamic_newline_programming._newline__newline_What this buys you._newline__newline_    • A single mathematical object (weakness as evidence) whose asymptotics yields LLC, and whose_newline_      algebra yields compositional control laws._newline__newline_                                                    3_newline_    • A rigorous model of “many approximate factorizations per context” as inference over a refinement_newline_      DAG._newline__newline_    • A clean bridge between: stagewise degeneracy changes in backprop Transformers; and the design_newline_      logic of causal-coding systems that maintain modularity and resist catastrophic forgetting under_newline_      shift._newline__newline__newline_2     A Systems Architecture: Base Learner + Structure Controller_newline_      + Meta-Controller_newline_2.1     The three loops (and why they are distinct)_newline_Informal picture.       We separate three time scales._newline__newline_ 1. Inference loop (fast): infer latent activities given input and current parameters. In predictive_newline_    coding this is a relaxation dynamics that reduces free energy._newline__newline_ 2. Learning loop (medium): update neural parameters (or program library) using local errors_newline_    and gates._newline__newline_ 3. Structure/Meta loop (slow): update modular factorization, gating policies, clarity strengths,_newline_    and shift segmentation so as to keep the system in a regime where continual-learning guarantees_newline_    hold._newline__newline_The thesis of this paper is that (3) can be formalized as inference and control on a refinement DAG,_newline_and that LLC/weakness provides a quantitative signal for when refactorization is needed._newline__newline_2.2     Formal system model_newline_Definition 1 (Contexts and data streams). Let C be a set of contexts (domains/tasks/interaction_newline_regimes). A nonstationary training process produces a time-indexed stream (ct , xt )t≥1 with ct ∈ C_newline_and xt ∼ Pct ._newline__newline_Definition 2 (Modular learner state). The learner state is modularized as_newline__newline_                                        Θ∼_newline_                                         = Θ(1) ⊗ · · · ⊗ Θ(K)_newline__newline_where Θ(k) is the parameter/state of module k (e.g. attention head, channel group, or program-block)._newline__newline_Definition 3 (Structure objects and refinement DAG). A factorization f is a choice of modular_newline_decomposition of the learner’s internal representation and/or parameters (not necessarily equal to_newline_the fixed physical module partition). Let F be a collection of candidate factorizations and let_newline__newline_                                              G = (F, E)_newline__newline_be a directed acyclic graph (DAG) whose edges represent refinement moves (e.g. splitting a module,_newline_introduc