mate MDL_newline_scoring. Later, the same interfaces can be implemented using Hyperon Atomspaces, MeTTa pattern_newline_matching, PLN-like inference, metagraph rewrite search, or other cognitive methods._newline_Design Principle 1 (Backend neutrality). The core CLA objects should not know how patterns_newline_were discovered. A chunk proposal may come from a Python n-gram counter, a SEQUITUR-like_newline_routine, an information-theoretic search, a Hyperon query, or a remote agent. The core induction_newline_loop should see all of these as typed Proposal objects._newline_Design Principle 2 (Optional Hyperon). Hyperon integration should be an optional adapter pack-_newline_age, not a core runtime dependency. The first implementation should be installable and testable_newline_without native Hyperon bindings, DAS, MeTTa, or any external Atomspace service._newline__newline__newline_4    Recommended Package Name_newline_Avoid a generic package name such as cla, which can collide with other meanings. Better choices_newline_are:_newline__newline_chaoslang_newline_chaosgram_newline_clalib_newline_chaos_language_newline__newline_    The rest of this document uses chaoslang._newline__newline__newline_5    Core Conceptual Model_newline_The library should expose a small number of central concepts._newline__newline_Corpus. A symbolic sequence, or a collection of sequences, with optional metadata about the_newline_    trajectory, source system, sampling interval, or partition._newline__newline_                                                   4_newline_Token. Something that can occur in a rewritten sequence. Tokens include base symbols, chunk_newline_    tokens, and category tokens._newline__newline_Base symbol. A token corresponding to an original cell in the symbolic partition._newline__newline_Chunk or nonterminal. A token defined by a production N → β, where β is a sequence of tokens._newline__newline_Meta-symbol or category. A token-like class defined by a member set M = {v