 "HUMAN_MESSAGE: " @bengoertzel: @Oruzibot @Protocosmobot @Protomegabot -- curious for feedback on this idea..._newline_[Telegram attachment: type=document, name=cetta_supercompilation_ascii.pdf, mime=application/pdf, size=149262, saved_path=/home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1783324217-file_31.pdf]_newline_<<<ATTACHMENT_TEXT_UNTRUSTED extracted_by=pdftotext>>>_newline_           CeTTa-Hosted Supercompilation for MeTTa:_newline_    A Human-Oriented Architecture with a Coding-Agent Appendix_newline_                                   Ben Goertzel + various AI tools_newline__newline_                                               July 5, 2026_newline__newline__newline_                                                 Abstract_newline_          This note summarizes a proposed synthesis of CeTTa, LeaTTa/Lean, MORK/PathMap,_newline_      MM2, and a multi-geometry intermediate representation for aggressive MeTTa supercompila-_newline_      tion. The central claim is that the right target is not simply “MeTTa compiled to MM2”, nor_newline_      “use PeTTa and let Prolog handle search”, nor “compile the standard library with MeTTaIL_newline_      and stop there”. The stronger architecture is a mixed system: CeTTa hosts generated C kernels_newline_      and indexed MORK artifacts; LeaTTa and Lean supply the semantic floor and certificate check-_newline_      ing; the multi-geometry IR chooses among native C, PathMap/trie, factor-graph, tensor, MM2,_newline_      and residual MeTTa presentations; and the runtime falls back to ordinary CeTTa evaluation_newline_      whenever guards fail._newline_          The body of the note is written for humans: concepts, motivations, semantic boundaries, and_newline_      high-level process. The appendix is written for coding agents: concrete work packets, interfaces,_newline_      guardrails, and anti-patterns._newline__newline__newline_1     Thesis_newline_The proposed architecture can be summarized as follows:_newline__newline_     Use LeaTTa/Lean to check what transformations mean. Use the multi-geometry IR to_newline_     decide what shape a hot computation should take. Use CeTTa to run the resulting spe-_newline_     cialized C kernels, PathMap/MORK artifacts, MM2 fragments, and residual MeTTa with_newline_     exact fallback._newline__newline_    This is intentionally different from three simpler plans._newline_    First, it is not “compile everything to MM2”. MM2 is valuable for monotone, pattern-heavy,_newline_sink-free execution, but it is not the only important computational geometry. Some hot regions_newline_want exact C control and native rematching. Some want PathMap prefix scans and trie joins._newline_Some want factor-graph demand/supply. Some want sparse or dense tensor kernels. Some must_newline_stay residual MeTTa because reflection or dynamic code generation is essential._newline_    Second, it is not “just use PeTTa”. PeTTa is excellent at Prolog-lineage backtracking search._newline_It is a crucial baseline and, for some workloads, plainly the best current engine. But it is not the_newline_natural host for zero-copy C kernels, MORK/PathMap artifacts, HE-profile conformance surfaces,_newline_C-level arena management, or mixed native/MM2 dispatch with manifest guards. The purpose_newline_here is not to replace PeTTa’s strengths; it is to recover the missing abstract-machine advantages_newline_inside a CeTTa host while also exploiting CeTTa’s C and MORK integration points._newline_    Third, it is not “just use MeTTaIL”. MeTTaIL-style contract-first boot compilation is comple-_newline_mentary and useful. But a supercompiler for large AI workloads needs runtime profile data, space_newline__newline_                                                     1_newline_schemas, effect and snapshot information, PathMap candidate contracts, C kernel loading, residual_newline_fallback, and revision guards. Those are runtime and artifact questions, not only boot-compilation_newline_questions._newline__newline__newline_2     Why CeTTa Adds Value_newline_CeTTa’s value in this design is not merely that it is written in C. Its value is that it sits at the_newline_right semantic and operational boundary. It is close enough to the HE MeTTa evaluator to serve_newline_as a compatibility host, low-level enough to host generated C kernels, and explicit enough about_newline_profiles, spaces, effects, and backends to make guarded supercompilation realistic._newline__newline_2.1   CeTTa as the execution host_newline_A supercompiled region should be loaded as an ordinary runtime capability, not as a forked lan-_newline_guage. CeTTa is well suited for this because it already has the shape of a direct evaluator rather_newline_than a compiler-only pipeline. A generated kernel can receive a CeTTa runtime context, access_newline_symbol identifiers, call native rematching, stream answers, allocate through arenas, and fall back_newline_to the interpreter when its manifest guards do not hold._newline_    At a high level, the target is:_newline__newline_MeTTa source + profile + workload statistics + space schemas_newline_        |_newline_        v_newline_Core normalization and effect analysis_newline_        |_newline_        v_newline_LeaTTa/Lean semantic checker and certificate layer_newline_        |_newline_        v_newline_MG-IR planner_newline_  - Native C presentation_newline_  - PathMap/trie presentation_newline_  - Factor-graph presentation_newline_  - Tensor presentation_newline_  - MM2 presentation_newline_  - Residual MeTTa presentation_newline_        |_newline_        v_newline_CettaPack artifact_newline_  - generated C shared object_newline_  - PathMap/MORK or .act artifacts_newline_  - optional MM2 fragments_newline_  - residual MeTTa fallback_newline_  - certificate and manifest guards_newline_        |_newline_        v_newline_CeTTa runtime dispatch with fallback_newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                 2_newline_   The key point is that CeTTa can be the place where these pieces meet in one process. PeTTa_newline_can run logic search well, and MeTTaIL can compile a contracted subset well, but CeTTa is the_newline_better host for a mixed native execution product._newline__newline_2.2    CeTTa provides a named semantic profile surface_newline_Supercompilation is dangerous when the source semantics are implicit. CeTTa’s profile family gives_newline_the optimizer a name for the semantic contract being specialized:_newline_   • he-compat: match upstream HE behavior, including quirks._newline_   • he: the principled line with recorded divergences._newline_   • he-extended: CeTTa extensions such as typed spaces, PathMap/MORK integration, and_newline_     snapshot surfaces._newline_   • he-prime: dependent telescope extensions._newline_   A supercompiled artifact must include the profile in its cache key and manifest guard. A kernel_newline_specialized under he-extended must not silently run under he-compat; a numeric or error-contour_newline_choice must not be hidden inside generated C. CeTTa’s explicit profile surface therefore becomes a_newline_practical safety mechanism._newline__newline_2.3    CeTTa has the right PathMap/MORK boundary_newline_The most important PathMap lesson is conservative:_newline_      PathMap should narrow candidates. CeTTa’s native matcher should remain the source_newline_      of truth for exact bindings, co-reference, binder hygiene, and result construction. Multi-_newline_      plicity should be carried by count metadata, not by distorting trie keys._newline_    This boundary is exactly what a supercompiler wants. For a hot match site, it can generate a_newline_site-specific query plan:_newline_1. Choose a selective PathMap prefix from grounded pattern parts._newline_2. Scan candidates or join several postings lists._newline_3. Call CeTTa native seeded rematch on each candidate._newline_4. Construct the result atom directly in C._newline_5. Stream answers to the continuation._newline_6. Fall back to generic match if any guard fails._newline_   This gives much of the performance benefit of deeper PathMap integration without replacing_newline_the evaluator’s exact semantics globally._newline__newline_2.4    CeTTa makes effects and mutation visible_newline_Supercompilation around nondeterminism and mutable spaces is not safe unless effects are explicit._newline_CeTTa’s sequential branch discipline, structured spaces, and snapshot extension give the optimizer_newline_useful hooks. A pure read-only query can be specialized aggressively. An append-only monotone_newline_loop can sometimes be lowered to MM2. A snapshot-isolated search can become a local episode._newline_A destructive shared-space mutation may need an optimization barrier._newline_    This is one reason a CeTTa-hosted supercompiler is more promising than a pure PeTTa or pure_newline_MM2 story. The system can use distinct machines for distinct semantic jobs:_newline__newline_                                                  3_newline_    • local search machine: choice frames, trail/rollback, scratch arenas;_newline__newline_    • indexed shared-space machine: PathMap/MORK, snapshots, epochs, tries, and joins;_newline__newline_    • type/elaboration machine: dependent binders, metavariables, and constraints;_newline__newline_    • MM2 machine: monotone forward saturation and priority scheduling._newline__newline__newline_3    The Role of LeaTTa and Lean_newline_LeaTTa should not be treated as the production execution backend for this proposal. Its best role_newline_is the semantic floor and cross-checking layer. The supercompiler should emit a certificate saying_newline_why the transformed MG-IR region is equivalent to, or safely approximates, the source region. Lean_newline_checks small transformation steps and backend contracts. CeTTa executes the resulting artifact._newline_    A useful certificate is not a full proof of arbitrary generated C