, priority schedul-_newline_                            ing_newline_      Residual MeTTa        reflective, dynamic, rare, or unsupported code_newline_    The planner chooses among these presentations after it sees profile information, effects, cache_newline_validity, space schemas, and exactness requirements. Humans provide the conceptual equivalences_newline_and laws; the compiler specializes within them._newline__newline__newline_5     Main Optimization Pattern 1: Match to PathMap Plan plus C_newline_      Rematch_newline_The first high-impact optimization should be a hot match compiler. Given a region such as:_newline_(match &kb (target rs10000544 $gene) $gene)_newline_    or a conjunction such as:_newline_(match &kb_newline_  (, (eqtl $snp $gene)_newline_     (has-disease $gene $disease)_newline_     (treats $drug $disease))_newline_  (drug-hypothesis $snp $drug $disease $gene))_newline_    the supercompiler emits a specialized kernel:_newline_kernel_match_site_173(ctx, demand, visitor)_newline_    The kernel is not a replacement for match. It is a compiled query plan for one site:_newline_    1. Load the guarded space schema and revision._newline_    2. Use grounded pattern parts to choose a PathMap prefix or trie path._newline_    3. If several patterns occur, use a product zipper or trie join._newline_    4. For each candidate, call exact CeTTa native seeded rematch._newline_    5. Construct the requested result in C._newline_    6. Stream each answer to the visitor._newline_    7. Preserve bag multiplicity using count metadata._newline_    8. Abort to generic CeTTa evaluation if any manifest guard fails._newline_   This pass alone addresses a major weakness: partial PathMap integration becomes site-specific,_newline_generated, and proof-guarded instead of requiring a risky global rewrite of the evaluator._newline__newline_                                                    5_newline_6    Main Optimization Pattern 2: Backward Chaining to a Local_newline_   