nd neighbors, and lower only appropriate monotone parts to MM2._newline_    This is the type of optimization humans should expose conceptually, not hard-code manually_newline_at every query. The human says: “this rule family admits proof search, factor demand/supply,_newline_saturation, and perhaps tensorization under these laws.” The compiler chooses the best presentation_newline_for the workload._newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                 6_newline_8    Main Optimization Pattern 4: Monotone Regions to MM2_newline_MM2 should be a late backend, not the universal immediate target. It is especially appropriate_newline_when the effect analysis proves that a region is append-only, monotone, and sink-free. Then the_newline_compiler can produce priority-scheduled forward rules and exploit persistent indices._newline_   A safe lowering path looks like this:_newline_MeTTa source_newline_  -> core/effect-normalized region_newline_  -> MG-IR monotone presentation_newline_  -> MM2 skeleton with priorities_newline_  -> CeTTa/MORK space execution via step!_newline_    An unsafe lowering is one that ignores destructive updates, hidden nondeterministic mutation,_newline_or branch-local state. Those regions should stay in native C, residual MeTTa, or a snapshot-isolated_newline_episode._newline__newline__newline_9    CettaPack: The Runtime Artifact_newline_A supercompiled region should be packaged as a loadable artifact with a manifest. A possible_newline_directory layout is:_newline_foo.cpack/_newline_  manifest.json_newline_  source_hash_newline_  profile_newline_  effect_summary_newline_  exactness_newline_  required_space_schema_newline_  required_space_revision_or_epoch_policy_newline_  pathmap_artifacts/_newline_    kb.act_newline_    query_indexes.pm_newline_  native/_newline_    libfoo_kernel.so_newline_  residual/_newline_    fallback.metta_newline_    hot.mm2_newline_  certs/_newline_    transform.cert_newline_    lean_ch