ewline__newline_1     Introduction_newline_Modern AI systems face a fundamental tension: they need the flexibility of high-level declarative_newline_languages for expressing complex reasoning, but require the performance of low-level implementations_newline_for production deployment. This tension occurs in many scenarios; three that we look at explicitly_newline_here are:_newline_   1. Knowledge-intensive reasoning: AI systems with large, fixed background knowledge bases_newline_       that must efficiently interpret new facts and queries_newline_   2. Evolutionary program synthesis: Genetic programming systems that repeatedly evaluate_newline_       candidate programs against fixed fitness functions_newline_   3. Hybrid symbolic-neural systems: Architectures combining high-level reasoning with_newline_       low-level pattern matching_newline_    This document presents a supercompiler design that addresses all three scenarios through_newline_selective, profile-guided specialization. The design maintains a minimal core IR with domain-specific_newline_features compiled to primitives, ensuring both theoretical cleanliness and practical implementability._newline__newline__newline_2     Design Principles and Architecture_newline_2.1   Core Design Principles_newline_Minimal Core IR. We maintain a tiny core intermediate representation containing only structural_newline_nodes. Domain-specific constructs (KB operations, evolutionary algorithms, MM2 integration)_newline_compile to this core plus primitive operations with effect metadata._newline__newline_                                                      1_newline_Formal Effect System. We define a complete effect algebra with commutativity rules, enabling_newline_provably safe reordering and speculation. Sink-free semantics are precisely specified as monotonic_newline_multiset additions._newline__newline_Query Planner Foundation. A query planner specifically designed for pattern-rewriting seman-_newline_tics (not SQL) provides the primary optimization layer. It handles cardinality estimation in MORK_newline_spaces, incremental statistics under monotonic growth, and effect-aware planning._newline__newline_Bounded Splitting. All splitting operations are statistics-guided with explicit bounds to prevent_newline_combinatorial explosion. We use symbolic splits by predicate/mode rather than fact enumeration._newline__newline_Canonical Keys. PathSig and SchemaKey use canonical encodings to prevent key explosion_newline_while ensuring sound folding. Subsumption relations are formally defined._newline__newline_Semantics-Preserving Compilation. MM2 compilation is proven correct through bisimulation._newline_Priority encoding of control flow has formal trace equivalence guarantees._newline__newline_2.2   System Architecture_newline_The system is organized in clean layers:_newline_  1. Surface Languages: MeTTa and MM2 with their native constructs_newline_  2. Domain IRs: KB-IR, Evo-IR, MM2-IR that capture domain semantics_newline_  3. Core IR: Minimal M-Core with only structural nodes_newline_  4. Query Planner: Pattern-rewriting aware optimization_newline_  5. Supercompiler: Selective application based on cost-benefit_newline_  6. Code Generation: To MM2 or native code_newline__newline__newline_3     M-Core: Minimal Core IR_newline_3.1   Core Node Types_newline_The core IR contains only essential structural nodes:_newline_   • Sym(name): Interned symbol_newline_   • Var(ix): Variable (de Bruijn or SSA indexed)_newline_   • Lit(val): Literal value_newline_   • Con(head:Sym, fields:[NodeID]): Constructor application_newline_   • App(fun:NodeID, args:[NodeID]): Function application_newline_   • Abs(params:[Var], body:NodeID): Abstraction_newline_   • Let(bindings:[(Var, NodeID)], body:NodeID): Let binding_newline_   • Match(scrut:NodeID, clauses:[(Pat, guard, body)]): Pattern match_newline_   • Choice(alts:[(guard, expr)]): Nondeterministic choice_newline_   • Prim(op:Sym, args:[NodeID]): Primitive operation_newline_   • Ref(def_id:Sym): Reference to definition_newline_   All nodes carry effect metadata but effects are not nodes themselves._newline__newline_3.2   Domain-Specific Compilation_newline_Domain constructs compile to core IR plus primitives:_newline__newline__newline_                                                2_newline_KB Operations._newline_KBFact(pred, args) -> Con(kb_fact, [Sym(pred), List(args)])_newline_KBQuery(pattern)   -> Prim(kb_query, [pattern], effects=[Read(kb)])_newline_KBRule(head, body) -> Abs([vars], Match(body, [(pat, True, head)]))_newline__newline_Evolution Operations._newline_FitnessEval(prog, data) -> Prim(fitness_eval, [prog, data],_newline_                                 effects=[Read(data), Observe(prog)])_newline_PopMember(id, fit, gen) -> Con(pop_member, [Lit(id), Lit(fit), gen])_newline__newline_MM2 Operations._newline_MM2Exec(pri, pats, temps) -> Prim(mm2_exec, [pri, pats, temps],_newline_                                   effects=[Read(space), Append(space)])_newline_MM2Pattern(expr) -> Con(mm2_pat, [expr])_newline__newline__newline_4     Formal Effect System_newline_4.1   Effect Algebra_newline_We define effects with precise semantics:_newline_Effect ::= Read(resource, scope)_newline_         | Write(resource, scope)_newline_         | Append(resource, scope)_newline_         | Create(resource)_newline_         | Delete(resource)_newline_         | Observe(resource)_newline_         | Pure_newline__newline_4.2   Commutativity Relations_newline_Effect commutativity is formally defined:_newline__newline_Algorithm 1 EffectCommutes_newline_ 1: function Commutes(effect1, effect2)_newline_ 2:    return match (effect1, effect2) with_newline_ 3:      (Pure, _) → true_newline_ 4:      (_, Pure) → true_newline_ 5:      (Read(r1,_), Read(r2,_)) → true_newline_ 6:      (Read(r1,_), Observe(r2)) → true_newline_ 7:      (Observe(r1), Observe(r2)) → true_newline_ 8:      (Append(r1,_), Append(r2,_)) → r1 6= r2_newline_ 9:      (Append(r,_), Read(r,_)) → false                       . Read sees appends_newline_10:      (Append(r,_), Observe(r)) → true                          . Observe doesn’t_newline_11:      (Write(r1,_), Write(r2,_)) → false_newline_12:      (Write(r,_), _) → false                             . Writes don’t commute_newline_13:      _ → false_newline_14: end function_newline__newline__newline_                                            3_newline_4.3     Sink-Free Semantics_newline_Formally, a program is sink-free if:_newline_  1. No Delete effects_newline_  2. All Write effects are idempotent (can be modeled as Append)_newline_  3. State changes are monotonic additions to multiset-valued stores_newline_  4. Guards are antimonotonic: if g holds in state s, then g holds in all s0 ⊇ s_newline_   Under sink-free semantics, we can safely:_newline_   • Share pattern matching results across time_newline_   • Build append-only indices_newline_   • Speculate without rollback_newline_   • Cache query results permanently_newline__newline__newline_5     Query Planner for Pattern-Rewriting Systems_newline_5.1     Cardinality Estimation in MORK Spaces_newline_5.1.1    Statistics Collection_newline_We maintain statistics specifically for MORK’s hash-consed structure:_newline__newline_Structure MORKStatistics {_newline_  node_type_counts: Map<NodeType, Count>_newline_  pattern_shape_histogram: PrefixTree<Shape, Count>_newline_  predicate_fanout: Map<Predicate, (avg_fanout, variance)>_newline_  argument_selectivity: Map<(Predicate, ArgPos), Histogram>_newline_  pattern_match_cache: LRU<PatternHash, MatchCount>_newline_  correlation_matrix: Map<(Pattern, Pattern), Float>_newline_}_newline__newline_5.1.2    Shape-Based Estimation_newline_Since MORK hash-conses, we exploit structural sharing for estimation:_newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                 4_newline_Algorithm 2 EstimatePatternCardinality_newline_ 1: function EstimateMatches(pattern, stats)_newline_ 2:    shape ← extract_shape(pattern, depth=3)_newline_ 3:    base_count ← stats.pattern_shape_histogram[shape]_newline_ 4:    if pattern has predicate then_newline_ 5:        pred ← pattern.predicate_newline_ 6:        fanout ← stats.predicate_fanout[pred].avg_newline_ 7:        base_count ← base_count * fanout_newline_ 8:        for (i, arg) in pattern.arguments do_newline_ 9:           if arg is constrained then_newline_10:                selectivity ← stats.argument_selectivity[(pred, i)]_newline_11:                base_count ← base_count * selectivity.estimate(arg)_newline_12:           end if_newline_13:        end for_newline_14:    end if_newline_15:    return (base_count, confidence_interval(stats, shape))_newline_16: end function_newline__newline__newline_5.1.3    Prefix-Tree Sampling_newline_MORK’s prefix structure enables efficient sampling:_newline__newline_Algorithm 3 PrefixSampling_newline_ 1: function SampleEstimate(pattern, space, sample_size)_newline_ 2:    prefix ← pattern.to_prefix(depth=2)_newline_ 3:    sample_size ← min(sample_size, sqrt(space.size))_newline_ 4:    sample ← uniform_sample_prefix(space, prefix, sample_size)_newline_ 5:    matches ← count_matches(pattern, sample)_newline_ 6:    estimate ← matches * (space.size / sample_size)_newline_ 7:    variance ← bootstrap_variance(matches, sample)_newline_ 8:    return (estimate, variance)_newline_ 9: end function_newline__newline__newline_5.2     Incremental Statistics Under Monotonic Growth_newline_5.2.1    Delta Statistics Maintenance_newline_Under sink-free semantics, statistics only grow:_newline__newline_Structure IncrementalStats {_newline_  base_statistics: MORKStatistics      // At last full scan_newline_  delta_statistics: MORKStatistics     // Since last scan_newline_  growth_rate: ExponentialAverage      // Facts/time_newline_  selectivity_drift: Map<Pattern, Float>_newline_  last_replan_time: Timestamp_newline_}_newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                   5_newline_Algorithm 4 UpdateIncrementalStats_newline_ 1: function UpdateStats(stats, new_facts)_newline_ 2:    for fact in new_facts do_newline_ 3:        shape ← extract_shape(fact)_newline_ 4:        stats.delta_statistics.pattern_shape_histogram[shape] += 1_newline_ 5:        if fact.is_predicate then_newline_ 6:            update_predicate_fanout(stats.delta_statistics, fact)_newline_ 7:            update_argument_selectivity(stats.delta_statistics, fact)_newline_ 8:        end if_newline_ 9:    end for_newline_10:    stats.growth_rate.update(len(new_facts))_newline_11:    if should_merge_delta(stats) then_newline_12:        merge_statistics(stats.base_statistics, stats.delta_statistics)_newline_13:        stats.delta_statistics ← empty_statistics()_newline_14:    end if_newline_15: end function_newline__newline__newline_5.2.2    Adaptive Replanning_newline_Replan when statistics drift significantly:_newline__newline_Algorithm 5 ShouldReplan_newline_ 1: function ShouldReplan(plan, current_stats)_newline_ 2:    threshold ← adaptive_threshold(current_stats.growth_rate)_newline_ 3:    for operation in plan.operations do_newline_ 4:        old_card ← operation.estimated_cardinality_newline_ 5:        new_card ← EstimateMatches(operation.pattern, current_stats)_newline_ 6:        drift ← abs(new_card - old_card) / old_card_newline_ 7:        if drift > threshold then_newline_ 8:            return true_newline_ 9:        end if_newline_10:    end for_newline_11:    time_since_replan ← now() - plan.creation_time_newline_12:    if time_since_replan > MAX_PLAN_AGE then_newline_13:        return true_newline_14:    end if_newline_15:    return false_newline_16: end function_newline__newline__newline_5.3     Effect-Aware Query Planning_newline_5.3.1    Planning with Effect Constraints_newline_The planner respects effect dependencies:_newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                  6_newline_Algorithm 6 EffectAwarePlanning_newline_ 1: function PlanQuery(query, stats, effect_analysis)_newline_ 2:    regions ← identify_pure_regions(query, effect_analysis)_newline_ 3:    plan ← []_newline_ 4:    for region in regions do_newline_ 5:        if region.is_pure then_newline_ 6:                                                        . Can reorder freely using cost model_newline_ 7:            local_plan ← cost_based_join_order(region, stats)_newline_ 8:        else_newline_ 9:                                                           . Must respect effect dependencies_newline_10:            deps ← build_dependency_graph(region)_newline_11:            local_plan ← topological_join_order(region, deps)_newline_12:        end if_newline_13:        if not region.is_pure then_newline_14:                                                        . Insert barrier to prevent reordering_newline_15:            plan.append(EffectBarrier(region.effects))_newline_16:        end if_newline_17:        plan.extend(local_plan)_newline_18:    end for_newline_19:    return optimize_plan(plan, stats)_newline_20: end function_newline__newline__newline_5.3.2    Effect Cost Modeling_newline_Track and estimate effect costs:_newline__newline_Structure EffectStats {_newline_  pattern_effect_probability: Map<PatternShape, Float>_newline_  effect_correlation: Map<(Pattern, Pattern), Float>_newline_  effect_cost: Map<EffectType, TimeCost>_newline_  effect_frequency: Map<(Pattern, Effect), Count>_newline_}_newline__newline__newline_6     Supercompiler Core with Minimal IR_newline_6.1     Structural Stepper_newline_The stepper is purely structural, calling domain functions through primitives:_newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                7_newline_Algorithm 7 RewriteOnce - Purely Structural_newline_ 1: function RewriteOnce(expr, env, deps)_newline_ 2:    effects ← analyze_effects(expr)_newline_ 3:                                       